From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] unidrv, unidrvui: a universal printer driver for GPD printers and their makers' plug-ins

Many makers' drivers are a GPD file (the printer's description: papers,
resolutions, the printer's commands) on Microsoft's Unidrv, often with a
render plug-in of their own: DYMO's LabelWriter 550 driver is lw550.gpd with
LW5XX.DLL (IPrintOemUni: ImageProcessing and FilterGraphics turn each page
into the 550's raster protocol, and it hooks DrvStartDoc, DrvStartPage,
DrvSendPage and DrvEndDoc to send the job header). Wine had no Unidrv, so
such a driver could not be installed. This is our own: unidrv.dll reads the
GPD (features, options, switches, macros, includes, commands with their
order and parameters), keeps the choices in its devmode beside the plug-in's
part, measures the page (DrvEnablePDEV's GDIINFO, landscape turned), sends
the job, document and page commands where Unidrv does, and turns each page
(or band) into raster rows -- through the plug-in's ImageProcessing and
FilterGraphics when it has them, else by the GPD's own commands with error
diffusion; the plug-in's DDI hooks wrap our entry points as on Windows.
unidrvui.dll answers DeviceCapabilities and DocumentProperties from the GPD
(a label printer's label stocks by their makers' names, from the resource
DLL). A plug-in that cannot load in the process (a 64-bit plug-in, a 32-bit
program) makes DrvEnablePDEV fail for printing, so the job is run by our
64-bit host (patch 0922).

Test: test/printdrv-gate.sh (Unidrv with our plug-in, and a GPD printer
without one; mutant SG_MUTANT_UNIOEM).
---
